s based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jonathan Laurence Steinberg | Founder, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 438 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $337K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["WisdomTree, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.8B market cap on $494M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $148M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 9.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","c